What:		/proc/jank_info/cpu_jank_info/sched_latency
What:		/proc/jank_info/cpu_jank_info/sched_iowait
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	4.14.357-openela-miru-h40
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read-only ColorOS 14 task-tracking event feeds.  Each file emits
		64 records followed by a blank line.  Records use the donor grammar:

		pid,duration_ns,realtime_seconds.realtime_nanoseconds

		`sched_latency` records runnable-to-running delays of at least 1 ms.
		`sched_iowait` records uninterruptible I/O-wait intervals of at
		least 1 ms.  Events are collected only for the four-PID task_track
		selection while task_track_enable is nonzero.  The implementation
		reuses the existing on-demand sched_switch and sched_waking
		tracepoints and two static 64-record rings.

		This batch deliberately does not register Binder, Futex, scheduler-
		tick, or stack-capture hooks.  The donor callstack and ux_throttle
		ABIs remain absent until their producers can be ported independently.
Users:		ColorOS performance diagnostics compatible with the OnePlus 9R
		Android 14 CPU-jank ABI.
